    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain clear of obstructions at all times could significantly improve emergency responder access to the main building and detached structure. Maintaining adequate vertical clearance and travel width along the driveway would support apparatus movement and turning near the structures. Clearly marking the property entrance from the street frontage may assist responding units in locating the access point quickly, particularly during low-visibility conditions. Where perimeter fencing intersects with potential secondary access corridors, ensuring gate hardware is compatible with emergency responder tools could facilitate movement around the property during rear-access operations."
